2026-10-20T11:37:44.6943220Z If you don't want to install the CLT, you can write appropriate configuration files pointing to your
2026-10-20T11:37:44.6946520Z SDK at ~/.config/clang.
2026-10-20T11:37:44.6947200Z 
2026-10-20T11:37:44.6954350Z To use the bundled libunwind please use the following LDFLAGS:
2026-10-20T11:37:44.6955850Z   LDFLAGS="-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/unwind -lunwind"
2026-10-20T11:37:44.6956530Z 
2026-10-20T11:37:44.6962890Z To use the bundled libc++ please use the following LDFLAGS:
2026-10-20T11:37:44.6964570Z   LDFLAGS="-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/c++ -L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/unwind -lunwind"
2026-10-20T11:37:44.6966370Z Features newer than system libc++ will require the following define to enable
2026-10-20T11:37:44.6967910Z (support for this may be removed in a future major LLVM release):
2026-10-20T11:37:44.6969090Z   CPPFLAGS="-D_LIBCPP_DISABLE_AVAILABILITY"
2026-10-20T11:37:44.6969560Z 
2026-10-20T11:37:44.6970850Z NOTE: You probably want to use the libunwind and libc++ provided by macOS unless you know what you're doing.
2026-10-20T11:37:44.6971910Z 
2026-10-20T11:37:44.6972730Z llvm is keg-only, which means it was not symlinked into /opt/homebrew,
2026-10-20T11:37:44.6986680Z because macOS already provides this software and installing another version in
2026-10-20T11:37:44.6988070Z parallel can cause all kinds of trouble.
2026-10-20T11:37:44.6988500Z 
2026-10-20T11:37:44.6989110Z If you need to have llvm first in your PATH, run:
2026-10-20T11:37:44.6990450Z   echo 'export PATH="/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/bin:$PATH"' >> /Users/runner/.bash_profile
2026-10-20T11:37:44.6991270Z 
2026-10-20T11:37:44.6991800Z For compilers to find llvm you may need to set:
2026-10-20T11:37:44.7000190Z   export LDFLAGS="-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib"
2026-10-20T11:37:44.7001420Z   export CPPFLAGS="-I/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/include"
2026-10-20T11:37:44.7002030Z 
